      { question: "Why does my USB-C dock only show one monitor on a MacBook?", answer: "Apple silicon MacBook Air and base M1 / M2 / M3 MacBooks support only one external display through DisplayPort Alt Mode, regardless of how many ports a dock has. Two displays require either a Pro / Max chip, a Thunderbolt dock with a supported dual-display engine, or a DisplayLink dock with the driver installed." },
